:name: CAN PoC step 2: one STM32F405, CAN1 -> CAN2
:description: CAN1 sends FLIGHT_PHASE (id 0x100) at 10 Hz, CAN2 receives it and prints it on USART2.
:
: how to run (from the top folder, the one with firmware/ and renode/):
:   make -C firmware
:   renode renode/f4_dual.resc then type: start
:   renode/run_can_tests.sh headless run with checks
:
: one machine (one chip), both of its CAN controllers on the same virtual bus:
:
:     +---------- f4 ----------+
:     |  can1 ----+            |
:     |           |  busA      |   busA is a Renode CANHub --> a virtual
:     |  can2 ----+            |   CAN bus with no wires and no bit timing
:     +------------------------+

using sysbus
$name?="f4"
mach create $name
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/stm32f405.repl

$elf?=@firmware/build/f4_dual.elf
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
    # flash isn't mirrored at address 0 here --> tell the CPU where the vector table is
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08000000
"""
runMacro $reset

# make the bus, then plug both controllers of this chip into it
# --> whatever can1 sends, can2 gets
emulation CreateCANHub "busA"
connector Connect sysbus.can1 busA
connector Connect sysbus.can2 busA

showAnalyzer usart2

include @renode/art/f4_dual.py
